From 009d3486512323b5879488fdb9c1b97be38621e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adeesababa <263047020+adeesababa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 03:33:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] NVR: RESZ depth resolve of a multisampled depth buffer takes
 the nearest sample (nvr.depthResolve)

The first sample of an MSAA depth buffer is whatever happened to cover it (with transparency multisampled grass: a blade or the
ground behind it, pixel by pixel), so the depth NVR rebuilds its normals and occlusion from was noisy along every grass edge
(the cloud-shadow crust on grass, the shadow ring round the player). ResolveZ now resolves the nearest sample: MIN for normal
depth, MAX for reversed depth, judged by the value that depth buffer was last cleared to (D3D9DeviceEx::Clear records it per
texture; sample 0 while it is not known). DxvkContext::resolveImage already falls back to its shader resolve where the device
cannot resolve MIN / MAX in a render pass. dxvk.conf nvr.depthResolve = sample0 restores the stock behaviour (default nearest).
Logs the mode once (and on each change).
